      "reason": "Clarify novelty, gate placement, and whether near-identity initialization introduces systematic forgetting.",
      "query": "Compare standard PyTorch GRU reset/update equations with h_t = GRUCell(x_t, sigmoid(W_x x_t + W_h h_previous + b) * h_previous). How does this extra gate change the recurrent carry path and gradients, what prior recurrent recommendation architectures use equivalent gating, and what initialization permits an exact identity-retention ablation?"
